---
title: Privacy Policy
description: "Last updated: 22 July 2026"
seoDescription: boXiv's Privacy Policy
---

This privacy policy describes how boXiv ("we", "us") handles information when you use boXiv (the "Site").

## Information we collect

### Account information

Creating an account is entirely optional. Browsing olympiad problems requires no sign-in. If you choose to sign in with GitHub, we receive

1. The information GitHub makes available by default (your GitHub username, display name and profile picture)
2. Your email address

We request **read-only access to your email address** and nothing else. We do not receive access to your repositories, followers/following, or any other GitHub data.

The information stored in our database when you create an account is:

- Your name and email address (as provided by GitHub)
- Your profile picture URL (as provided by GitHub)
- The date your boXiv account is created
- Your account role (default: user)

## How we use your information

We use your account information solely to:

- Identify you when you sign in
- Gate access to contributor features (adding or editing olympiad content)
- Allow administrators to manage user accounts

We do not sell, share, or transfer your personal information to any third party for marketing or commercial purposes.

## Data retention

Your account data is retained for as long as your account exists. You may request deletion of your account and associated data at any time by contacting us via the [GitHub repository](https://github.com/darshdudhia/boxiv).

## Third-party services

The Site is hosted on [Vercel](https://vercel.com), and account data is stored in a [Neon](https://neon.tech) Postgres database. Authentication is handled via [GitHub OAuth](https://docs.github.com/en/apps/creating-github-apps/authenticating-with-a-github-app/authenticating-with-a-github-app-on-behalf-of-a-user); you will be redirected to GitHub's own sign-in page and are subject to [GitHub's privacy statement](https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement) during that process.

## Cookies

The only cookie we set is the session cookie [BetterAuth](https://better-auth.com) generates to keep you signed in. No advertising or tracking cookies are used.

## Contact

If you have any questions about this policy, please reach out via the [GitHub repository](https://github.com/darshdudhia/boxiv).
